{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01K78mk7ASEy8JLqVsPaWAeR","type":"tool_result","content":"185\t/// was written (by either `.so`, through libc's buffered `stdout`).\n186\tfn capture<F: FnOnce()>(f: F) -> Vec<u8> {\n187\t    let _guard = capture_lock();\n188\t    let path = temp_path();\n189\t    let file = File::create(&path).expect(\"create capture file\");\n190\t\n191\t    unsafe {\n192\t        // Flush anything already pending so it lands on the real stdout.\n193\t        fflush(null_mut());\n194\t    }\n195\t    let saved = unsafe { dup(STDOUT_FD) };\n196\t    assert!(saved >= 0, \"dup(1) failed\");\n197\t    assert!(\n198\t        unsafe { dup2(file.as_raw_fd(), STDOUT_FD) } >= 0,\n199\t        \"dup2 onto stdout failed\"\n200\t    );\n201\t\n202\t    f();\n203\t\n204\t    unsafe {\n205\t        // Force libc to drain the stdout buffer into the temp file *before* the\n206\t        // redirection is undone.\n207\t        fflush(null_mut());\n208\t        assert!(dup2(saved, STDOUT_FD) >= 0, \"restoring stdout failed\");\n209\t        close(saved);\n210\t    }\n211\t    drop(file);\n212\t\n213\t    let out = std::fs::read(&path).expect(\"read capture file\");\n214\t    let _ = std::fs::remove_file(&path);\n215\t    assert_uncontaminated(&out);\n216\t    out\n217\t}\n218\t\n219\t/// Safety net for the capture mechanism itself.\n220\t///\n221\t/// fd 1 is process-wide, so if the tests were ever run concurrently, libtest's\n222\t/// own `test <name> ... ok` progress lines would be written into the capture and\n223\t/// silently corrupt every comparison. The libraries under test can only ever\n224\t/// emit `[0-9a-f]` and `'\\n'`, so anything else means the capture was polluted.\n225\t/// `.cargo/config.toml` forces `RUST_TEST_THREADS=1` to prevent this; this check\n226\t/// makes a mis-invocation fail loudly instead of producing bogus results.\n227\t#[track_caller]\n228\tfn assert_uncontaminated(out: &[u8]) {\n229\t    if let Some(pos) = out\n230\t        .iter()\n231\t        .position(|c| !(c.is_ascii_digit() || (b'a'..=b'f').contains(c) || *c == b'\\n'))\n232\t    {\n233\t        panic!(\n234\t            \"stdout capture was polluted at offset {pos} (byte {:#04x}); \\\n235\t             run the tests single-threaded (RUST_TEST_THREADS=1 / \\\n236\t             `-- --test-threads=1`). Captured prefix: {:?}\",\n237\t            out[pos],\n238\t            String::from_utf8_lossy(&out[..out.len().min(200)])\n239\t        );\n240\t    }\n241\t    assert_eq!(\n242\t        out.len() % REC,\n243\t        0,\n244\t        \"stdout capture length {} is not a multiple of the 9-byte record size; \\\n245\t         the capture was polluted -- run the tests single-threaded\",\n246\t        out.len()\n247\t    );\n248\t}\n249\t\n250\tfn capture_c(bits: &[u32]) -> Vec<u8> {\n251\t    let f = libs().c_driver;\n252\t    capture(|| {\n253\t        for &b in bits {\n254\t            unsafe { f(f32::from_bits(b)) };\n255\t        }\n256\t    })\n257\t}\n258\t\n259\tfn capture_rust(bits: &[u32]) -> Vec<u8> {\n260\t    let f = libs().r_driver;\n261\t    capture(|| {\n262\t        for &b in bits {\n263\t            unsafe { f(f32::from_bits(b)) };\n264\t        }\n265\t    })\n266\t}\n267\t\n268\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n269\t// comparison\n270\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n271\t\n272\tfn model_record(bits: u32) -> String {\n273\t    let b = f32::from_bits(bits).to_bits().to_ne_bytes();\n274\t    format!(\"{:02x}{:02x}{:02x}{:02x}\\n\", b[0], b[1], b[2], b[3])\n275\t}\n276\t\n277\tfn show(rec: &[u8]) -> String {\n278\t    String::from_utf8_lossy(rec).escape_debug().to_string()\n279\t}\n280\t\n281\t/// The core assertion used by every Phase B / Phase C row.\n282\t///\n283\t/// * captures BOTH `.so`s' output for the same input list,\n284\t/// * asserts the streams are byte-identical,\n285\t/// * asserts the 9-byte framing invariant (`ERRORS.md` row 11 / `CONFIGS.md`\n286\t///   row 22) and the lowercase-hex character set,\n287\t/// * cross-checks the C output against an independent model of\n288\t///   `printf(\"%02x\")` over the argument's object representation, which would\n289\t///   catch a harness bug (e.g. a value mangled on its way through the FFI call)\n290\t///   masking a real divergence.\n291\t#[track_caller]\n292\tfn assert_same(row: &str, bits: &[u32]) {\n293\t    assert!(!bits.is_empty(), \"{row}: empty input list\");\n294\t    let c_out = capture_c(bits);\n295\t    let r_out = capture_rust(bits);\n296\t\n297\t    assert_eq!(\n298\t        c_out.len(),\n299\t        bits.len() * REC,\n300\t        \"{row}: C emitted {} bytes for {} calls, expected {} (9 per call)\",\n301\t        c_out.len(),\n302\t        bits.len(),\n303\t        bits.len() * REC\n304\t    );"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1b4c23cf-76e2-454f-8a84-8d4383224b9e","uuid":"aa1e336b-8e31-46a0-a6ce-794b53225151","timestamp":"2026-08-18T11:24:59.763Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-eVa0F8/translated_rust/tests/differential.rs","content":"/// was written (by either `.so`, through libc's buffered `stdout`).\nfn capture<F: FnOnce()>(f: F) -> Vec<u8> {\n    let _guard = capture_lock();\n    let path = temp_path();\n    let file = File::create(&path).expect(\"create capture file\");\n\n    unsafe {\n        // Flush anything already pending so it lands on the real stdout.\n        fflush(null_mut());\n    }\n    let saved = unsafe { dup(STDOUT_FD) };\n    assert!(saved >= 0, \"dup(1) failed\");\n    assert!(\n        unsafe { dup2(file.as_raw_fd(), STDOUT_FD) } >= 0,\n        \"dup2 onto stdout failed\"\n    );\n\n    f();\n\n    unsafe {\n        // Force libc to drain the stdout buffer into the temp file *before* the\n        // redirection is undone.\n        fflush(null_mut());\n        assert!(dup2(saved, STDOUT_FD) >= 0, \"restoring stdout failed\");\n        close(saved);\n    }\n    drop(file);\n\n    let out = std::fs::read(&path).expect(\"read capture file\");\n    let _ = std::fs::remove_file(&path);\n    assert_uncontaminated(&out);\n    out\n}\n\n/// Safety net for the capture mechanism itself.\n///\n/// fd 1 is process-wide, so if the tests were ever run concurrently, libtest's\n/// own `test <name> ... ok` progress lines would be written into the capture and\n/// silently corrupt every comparison. The libraries under test can only ever\n/// emit `[0-9a-f]` and `'\\n'`, so anything else means the capture was polluted.\n/// `.cargo/config.toml` forces `RUST_TEST_THREADS=1` to prevent this; this check\n/// makes a mis-invocation fail loudly instead of producing bogus results.\n#[track_caller]\nfn assert_uncontaminated(out: &[u8]) {\n    if let Some(pos) = out\n        .iter()\n        .position(|c| !(c.is_ascii_digit() || (b'a'..=b'f').contains(c) || *c == b'\\n'))\n    {\n        panic!(\n            \"stdout capture was polluted at offset {pos} (byte {:#04x}); \\\n             run the tests single-threaded (RUST_TEST_THREADS=1 / \\\n             `-- --test-threads=1`). Captured prefix: {:?}\",\n            out[pos],\n            String::from_utf8_lossy(&out[..out.len().min(200)])\n        );\n    }\n    assert_eq!(\n        out.len() % REC,\n        0,\n        \"stdout capture length {} is not a multiple of the 9-byte record size; \\\n         the capture was polluted -- run the tests single-threaded\",\n        out.len()\n    );\n}\n\nfn capture_c(bits: &[u32]) -> Vec<u8> {\n    let f = libs().c_driver;\n    capture(|| {\n        for &b in bits {\n            unsafe { f(f32::from_bits(b)) };\n        }\n    })\n}\n\nfn capture_rust(bits: &[u32]) -> Vec<u8> {\n    let f = libs().r_driver;\n    capture(|| {\n        for &b in bits {\n            unsafe { f(f32::from_bits(b)) };\n        }\n    })\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// comparison\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nfn model_record(bits: u32) -> String {\n    let b = f32::from_bits(bits).to_bits().to_ne_bytes();\n    format!(\"{:02x}{:02x}{:02x}{:02x}\\n\", b[0], b[1], b[2], b[3])\n}\n\nfn show(rec: &[u8]) -> String {\n    String::from_utf8_lossy(rec).escape_debug().to_string()\n}\n\n/// The core assertion used by every Phase B / Phase C row.\n///\n/// * captures BOTH `.so`s' output for the same input list,\n/// * asserts the streams are byte-identical,\n/// * asserts the 9-byte framing invariant (`ERRORS.md` row 11 / `CONFIGS.md`\n///   row 22) and the lowercase-hex character set,\n/// * cross-checks the C output against an independent model of\n///   `printf(\"%02x\")` over the argument's object representation, which would\n///   catch a harness bug (e.g. a value mangled on its way through the FFI call)\n///   masking a real divergence.\n#[track_caller]\nfn assert_same(row: &str, bits: &[u32]) {\n    assert!(!bits.is_empty(), \"{row}: empty input list\");\n    let c_out = capture_c(bits);\n    let r_out = capture_rust(bits);\n\n    assert_eq!(\n        c_out.len(),\n        bits.len() * REC,\n        \"{row}: C emitted {} bytes for {} calls, expected {} (9 per call)\",\n        c_out.len(),\n        bits.len(),\n        bits.len() * REC\n    );","numLines":120,"startLine":185,"totalLines":893}}}
